 "result_text": "I changed `partition_asymmetry` in `neurom/features/bifurcation.py` so the Uylings variant no longer raises when both child subtrees are single tips. I haven't run it or any tests.\n\nWith `uylings=True`, a bifurcation whose two children are both leaves has `n + m = 2`. The old code raised `NeuroMError` there, so any morphology with a terminal bifurcation would fail. Uylings' formula, |n\u2212m| / (n+m\u22122), is 0/0 in that case. It now returns 0.0 instead, which is the symmetric case. The `NeuroMError` import is still used elsewhere in the file.\n\n`n` and `m` are still counted as nodes in each child subtree, as before. Uylings defines them as terminal tips, which is a separate question I left alone.",
